WEBVTT

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.340
Why?

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.850
Why would the Devil <i>save</i> people?

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.610
<i>Right here, this moment,</i> <i>this is our starting point</i>

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:39.660
<i>Let's picture what we might be able to do</i>

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:43.710
<i>Unbelievable things can happen sometimes</i>

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:49.420
<i>More... we can push past this</i>

00:00:50.960 --> 00:01:00.310
<i>Everything is born from zero;</i>
<i>I want to shine, flap my wings hard</i>

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.770
<i>And fly to that sky</i>

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:11.940
<i>Come on, let's go, with</i> <i>brilliant smiles on our faces!</i>

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:17.740
<i>Let's fly off to an unknown world right now</i>

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:22.410
<i>I decide, I'm the one who chooses my future</i>

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.790
<i>Let's follow our dreams</i>

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.330
<i>Sure, some days we'll cry</i>

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:32.630
<i>It's a precious wish, don't disappear</i>

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:40.560
<i>I'm going after the future you,</i> <i>because I know I'll find you</i>

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.650
I'm reporting from a helicopter above the site of Shinjuku's subway collapse.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.900
There are plenty of emergency vehicles on the scene

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.660
and the atmosphere is solemn, but to everyone's shock,

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.490
despite the magnitude of the disaster, there are no casualties.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.250
I repeat: We've been informed that there are no casualties. The police--

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.790
Daddy!

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.550
Daddy!

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.670
I brought lunch!

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:20.050
Thank you, Emilia.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.520
Is it good?

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.270
Yep!

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.190
Hey there Nord, Emilia.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:30.400
Wow, Emilia, did you make that?

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:31.520
Yes!

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:32.940
I bet it's good!

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.320
Uh-huh!

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:38.320
You can have some, too.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.740
Well, that's mighty kind.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:48.920
Did you hear? The eastern and northern lands fell to the Devil's army.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.290
Everybody's saying the West will be next.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:58.760
We're completely safe protected by the
Grand Hoshin Church and the Royal Army.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.220
There's nothing to worry about.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:05.810
Well, I think we'd be helpless facing the demon general Lucifer!

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.560
Times are bad, if you ask me.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.150
Are demons coming here?

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:17.360
It's okay. The holy father's prayers will protect us.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.490
Don't you worry.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.120
Daddy's right, you know!

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.910
Because Daddy never lies!

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.700
Right, Daddy?

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.330
Nope, he sure doesn't. You're exactly right.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.720
Holy father?

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:48.390
Did you come to save us from the demons?

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.560
Daddy!

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:58.110
The holy father came to save the village!

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.880
Emilia... he came to take you with him.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.710
Huh? Why?

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.300
This is the day I've been protecting you for.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.590
Daddy?

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.930
You're an angel's child.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:29.770
The only human in Ente Isla with the power to defeat the Devil.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:34.190
What? No. I'm <i>your</i> child, Daddy.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.480
Yes. And you're also your angel mother's child.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:43.490
I don't understand! I don't get what you're saying, Daddy!

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.160
You will.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:52.750
What about you? You're coming with us, right?

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.630
I'm sorry.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:02.670
I pray you'll lead a life full of light, in a world swept clean of evil.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:07.470
Emilia, my daughter...
I love you with all my heart.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:13.890
That was the last time I ever saw my father.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:17.060
Several days after I was separated from him,

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.110
our village was burned to ashes

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:23.490
by the demon army sent to crush the West, led by general Lucifer.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.830
Do not lose heart, Emilia.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:38.170
You have inherited the power of your mother, one of the great angels.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:41.800
Now, listen: the sacred evolving sword "Better Half"

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:46.880
is a holy weapon that only children of both a human and an angel can wield.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:48.510
You are the...

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:53.270
...only human in Ente Isla with the power to defeat the Devil.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:57.100
Then please teach me to sword-fight.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:00.570
So that I can defeat the Devil myself.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:01.570
How dare you?!

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:02.980
Well, you were out of it,

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:07.070
like your life was flashing before your eyes, so I wondered if you were okay.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:11.370
I'm fine! And <i>you</i> don't get to worry about me.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.460
You're back to your sloppy self!

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.170
The "sloppy" was uncalled for.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.580
Mr. Maou!

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:19.420
Chi.

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:21.750
Um, I...

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:24.550
Aw, I'm just glad you're okay.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.300
R-Right...

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:29.840
Kids, it's dangerous over there, so come-- Hmm?

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:32.720
Say, are you Inspector Sasaki's daughter?

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:38.600
Oh, Senichi Sasaki at West
Shinjuku Station is my father, yes...

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:44.780
I knew I recognized you! I'll go get him.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.610
U-Um, Mr. Maou...

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:51.200
I get it, don't worry.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.120
No girl wants to get mixed up in a crisis on a date,

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.370
even if nothing sketchy happened, right?

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:57.750
It's even worse for me!

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.000
I'm sorry.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.580
Nah, don't sweat it. See you tomorrow!

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:03.000
Yes!

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:05.800
Thank you, too, Miss Yusa.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.090
Sasaki from West Shinjuku Station, eh?

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.050
It's no coincidence, then.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.680
The magic I used when I first got here affected his daughter

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:17.230
and made her hear that voice.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:18.730
What's your plan?

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:22.770
Eat in a bunch of underground cafés and wait for one to collapse.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.070
Are you stupid?

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.150
Can it, you.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.400
I'm tired. I'm gonna go home and sleep.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:29.990
Hey!

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.990
Nothing else is gonna happen for today.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.540
Their attack failed, after all.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:36.620
Failed?

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.160
Yeah. That was no natural quake.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:45.040
It happened when we were in the same place, meaning somebody set us up.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:48.970
I don't know if they used a sonar pulse or magical interference,

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:53.470
but one thing's for sure: our covers are blown.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:54.930
Then our enemy...

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.060
Has been standing right next to us.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.600
Maybe the reason he didn't follow up

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.150
is because my magic started to come back?

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:05.480
But who could it be, then?!

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.530
Who could put out so much power here in Japan,

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.570
--where we can't replenish magic or celestial force--
--Emi! Emi!

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:14.070
--Emi! Over here!
--Rika?!

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.410
--Hey, Emi, are you okay?!
--Wow, you actually have a friend.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.620
--Emi, hey!
--What do you care?!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:19.870
--Emi!
--Go on, she's waiting.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:21.830
--Emi, listen!
--I know that!

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.830
Hurry up!

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.960
Emi, thank goodness!

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:26.630
See you later.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.670
Your Majesty!

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.300
What now?

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.930
I'm so sorry, Sire! Not only did I allow Emilia near you,

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.550
but I didn't notice the enemy closing in!

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:41.560
And then I put you in a position to save my life! How can I ever apologize?!

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.390
Quit crying. We're going home.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.610
You're not hurt, right?

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:49.070
You even graciously inquire after my welfare! I...

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:52.280
--Don't cling to me! It's creepy! Cut it out!
--Sire!

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.740
Oh, so your parents live abroad?

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:58.740
Yeah, essentially...

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.120
Sorry for crashing, though.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.540
No, I'm sorry for dragging you here!

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.290
Oh, you didn't drag me!

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.960
It's just... hmm...

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:14.720
Going by my own experience,
I figured maybe you shouldn't be alone.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.930
Here you go! You missed dinner, right?

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:23.140
Yep. These hunger pains feel more deadly than the cave-in!

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:25.520
Okay, eat up, then!

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:30.520
Sire, please punish me!

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.190
I told you, just forget about it!

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.910
Could I have a word with you two?

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.530
Phew, thanks for the food!

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:44.040
If you're <i>that</i> hungry, I guess
I don't need to worry about you.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.250
Nope!

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.540
Excuse me a second.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.170
Hello!

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.670
Ah, ya got it?

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:58.550
Nah, it ain't 'spensive, and Grampa loves all <i>shochu</i>, yeah?

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.430
Today's quake? Nothin' to worry about.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:06.850
'S close to work, but I'm safe, so let everybody know, yeah?

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.400
'Kay, bye!

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.730
That was Mama.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:11.940
--Her?
--Yep!

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:15.110
I've never heard you use that dialect before.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.240
I grew up in Kobe.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:21.580
But it's always a hassle talking about where I'm from, so I don't.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.330
A hassle how?

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:26.370
People think they can ask me all these questions.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.080
About the earthquake, and stuff.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:34.170
I was little then, but I still can't forget it.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:37.170
It was... really scary.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:42.390
People have asked me lots of things that were hard to answer.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:46.560
Hard to answer...

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:57.110
What? What's with the sudden hug?

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.740
You're the first one, Emi.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.160
Huh?

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:06.410
The first person not to ask insensitive questions when I say I'm from Kobe.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.540
When a person's outlook gets turned upside-down,

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:13.170
you never know which way they'll go.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:18.340
Some people take advantage of the chaos to do bad things, you know.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.890
And other people are so soft-hearted,

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:25.310
they'll do anything to help you, even after they've lost everything.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.720
So I thought...

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.560
You know how when you feel torn,

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:33.310
it's like your angel and demon selves are arguing?

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.650
I thought, "People can turn either angel or demon, if they decide to."

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:42.110
Either angel or demon...?

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.830
You boys are with an acting troupe, right?

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:45.450
--Huh?
--What?

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:49.250
I used to want to be an actor, so I know where you're coming from.

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:52.210
But no practicing your lines on the sidewalk, okay?

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:53.080
Er...

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:58.130
I'm sure it's tough selling your ticket quotas and whatnot, but keep at it.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:02.050
Maybe this doesn't mean much from a man whose dream never came true,

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:04.300
but the minute you give up, it's all over.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:05.600
Right...

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:07.430
Oh, and watch out!

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:13.100
Lots of muggings around here lately, and you don't want people suspecting you!

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.820
Emi, you can take the first bath.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:24.370
Oh, okay.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:29.120
A salaryman had his briefcase stolen on the way home from work.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:33.120
--From the MO, the police suspect that

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:31.120
--Ugh, again?!

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.120
--Lots of those lately, huh?

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:35.040
--Times like these make a girl wish
--this was the work of the same man

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:38.500
--she had someone to play bodyguard!
--behind the recent string of muggings.

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:40.510
You're lucky there, Emi.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:41.260
Huh?

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:44.260
You know, that guy you were talking with before.

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:45.180
That jerk isn't--

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:47.810
So you're close enough to call each other "jerk"?

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:52.060
He looked pretty fine.
I can't help but be curious!

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:56.440
That je-- That guy is nothing to me!

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:59.440
I'll put some towels out here!

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:01.360
Okay, thanks!

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:11.080
What's this feeling... this warmth?

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.080
Is this the human heart?

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:23.300
If so, what was <i>he</i> thinking when he saved those people?

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:29.680
What do you want? It's early.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:35.020
Don't worry, it's not poison or razor blades or anything.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:39.110
Can't think of any reason I'd get something <i>not</i> dangerous from you...

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:42.990
Oh, does that mean I can keep the 1,000 yen?

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.780
Now we're even.

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:50.660
Hey! What about your promise to leave us alone for a while?!

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:54.210
I agreed to be your guarantor, so we're square!

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:55.500
Why, you--

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:58.790
Was Alciel okay in the cave-in?

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:03.760
Well, he ain't injured. Seems to have taken a psychological hit, though.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:04.300
Huh?

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:08.090
Your Majesty! Please forgive me!

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:12.010
--He knew I'd gotten a little power back...
--I am a vile, useless demon!

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:15.730
...but he still beat himself up all night

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:20.230
for not being able to do anything for his king in crisis, so he's sleeping in.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:21.860
Sheesh...

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:25.030
So what about you? Are you okay?

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:29.110
You used your power to put Chi to sleep, right?

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:32.620
I-I'm not so far gone I need an enemy worrying about me!

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:36.290
Oh? Fine, then. If you're done, feel free to scram.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.540
That's the plan!

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.380
It's too early for this...

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.630
Hey, Emi! Those shoes don't have the traction for--

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:47.470
An enemy attack?!

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:54.560
Well, I never! For the hero who very nearly vanquished King Satan

00:14:54.770 --> 00:15:00.400
to sustain so many injuries falling down the stairs, even in an assumed form,

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:04.110
simply injures His Majesty's reputation!

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:09.530
Hmm, we only have adhesive bandages.
Did we never buy gauze?

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:13.410
Oh, well. I know it's a pain, but make a quick trip to the pharmacy

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:15.540
and buy her some gauze and bandages.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:18.790
I don't want her carping at me again.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.580
As you wish, Sire.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.500
Might I borrow Dullahan, then?

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:25.050
Permission granted.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.300
Might as well at least disinfect it now...

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:30.970
Use this to--

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.720
D-Don't touch me!

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.260
I can do it myself!

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.930
Yeah, yeah, excuse <i>me.</i>

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:38.770
Here, have at it.

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:43.520
Does it sting?

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:44.980
No!

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:49.360
--Hey! What was that for?!
--Shut up!

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:52.320
What are <i>you</i> doing?! You're the Devil, right?!

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:56.120
So act like it! Commit every atrocity you can think of in this world!

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.450
What? Where did <i>that</i> come from?!

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:00.790
What's with you?! You're poor, you cook your own meals,

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:04.340
you're respected at your job, you work your wiles on high school girls--

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:08.590
I've never heard of a Devil being vain just because some teenager likes him!

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:12.180
--One of those things was not like the others.
--I think the shoe fits!

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:18.180
Well, <i>I've</i> never seen a hero who fell down the stairs, cried, and got patched up by demons!

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:24.520
Why are you nice to me?

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:25.190
Huh?

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:31.280
Why are you nice to me... to people... to this world?

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:34.450
Why can you be so nice?!

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:37.370
If you can be nice, then why...

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:40.700
Why did you kill my father?!

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:46.630
The Devil I know is cruel, and he kills humans as easily as bugs,

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:51.590
and he's happiest when the world is filled with sorrow and blood!

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:52.130
I--

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:55.930
You burned our fields with fire-- you destroyed our castles with lightning--

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:57.930
You swept away our towns with floods!

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:01.850
You're Satan, ruler of demons, and you allow them any brutality!

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:05.150
I swear on my life, I'll never forgive you!

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:10.570
Our house, my father's fields, my father's life--

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:14.410
You stole every bit of my peaceful existence from me!

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:17.490
I'll never forgive you!

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:24.580
I've never thought too much about it, but...

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:28.170
Sorry, I guess.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:33.170
I didn't really understand humans, back then.

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:34.970
Good morning!

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:41.220
I ran into Miss Sasaki, and she said she'd like to see you--

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:50.610
Oh, I-I... You two really... y-you really <i>are</i>, aren't you?

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:51.940
Ch-Chi?

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:54.070
Ch-Chiho! It's not what it looks like!

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:55.740
I-I'm sorry!

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:56.990
Chi!

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.330
This is bad, huh.

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:06.540
A lovers' quarrel with his old girl over a beautiful new one...

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:09.750
And then the new girl herself arrives on the scene

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:14.630
and discovers he never really broke things off with his ex.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:20.850
This is the sort of sordid romantic drama syrupy enough to cause heart disease.

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:22.390
What?! Is it really?

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:23.350
Not you, too...

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:27.520
I am Miki Shiba, the landlady of this establishment.

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:30.480
I take it you are Mr. Maou's girlfriend?

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:32.270
M-Me, with <i>this</i> loser?!

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:33.230
"Loser"?!

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.200
--Um, Ms. Shi--
<i>--Non</i>! "Mikitty," please.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.910
Uh, right...

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:41.580
You see, I'm having some repairs done to these apartments.

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:45.620
I'm informing the tenants now.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:50.420
There are so many disturbing goings-on these days, yes? Cave-ins and such.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:51.630
Y-Yes...

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:54.880
I wonder if something will happen again today?

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:56.880
I-I'm sure I couldn't say...

00:18:57.090 --> 00:19:00.340
That reminds me, that adorable young lady who was just here

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:03.970
seems to have run off toward the train station in tears.

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:07.810
The ground shook...?

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:09.560
Mr. Maou.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:13.070
If you've involved her, I hope you'll take full responsibility.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:14.270
F-For what?

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:18.030
Surely you've realized by now that it was no coincidence

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.950
when that adorable girl took a direct sonar hit

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:24.410
and received an idea link transmission?

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:27.790
Don't you three know better than anyone else

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:32.040
that thought and will have great power?

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:36.760
I warn you, if you do not hurry, you may be too late.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.840
Ms. Shiba...?

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:44.600
I feel gross! I think I'm going to be Gate-sick!

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.060
Keep it together, please!

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:51.350
It seems we won't have time to rest when we get there.

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:54.480
You've picked up something?

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:58.690
I detect artificial magic on a scale unsupportable

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:06.990
by the "Japanese" magical reserves
I calculated from sonar measurements.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:09.580
Is Emilia in trouble?

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:11.580
It's possible.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:14.840
Perhaps we'd better prepare for a fight.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.670
Got it.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.590
Hurry, then. I can take it.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:19.880
Understood.

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:22.630
Here we goooo!

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:25.050
Try not to shake me!

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:32.440
Huh? Why am I crying?

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:38.860
I must love Mr. Maou after all.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:42.240
I'm sorry.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:45.120
Well, well, you'll make a fine meal.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:50.950
I've been watching you since my earlier failure, just in case,

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:55.420
but I never dreamed you'd fall prey to despair so <i>easily.</i>

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:57.920
Chiho Sasaki.

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:02.090
I shall feed on your bitterness and despair over the Devil and the hero,

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:04.760
and materialize here.

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:06.390
Hey, don't just stand there--

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:15.850
Now then, it's time for the hunt.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:18.480
Today I shall surpass the ruler of demons.

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:25.200
This is horrible!

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:27.950
Him...!

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.750
Who is that? Did he do this?!

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:33.330
Isn't that obvious?

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:45.090
Heh, I knew it.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:46.340
It can't be!

00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:49.140
My, my, if it isn't the great King Satan--

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:53.640
--or should I call you Sadao Maou now?

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:57.100
And what exactly are <i>you</i> doing here,

00:21:57.310 --> 00:22:00.690
demon general Lucifer?

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:23.460
<i>Where will morning start from, in this quiet sky?</i>

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:29.090
<i>Fingertips twining in a pinky</i> <i>swear I pretended not to see</i>

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:39.300
<i>If the moon's been laughed at,</i> <i>she'll sink away toward yesterday</i>

00:22:39.980 --> 00:22:45.240
<i>Liar, coward--if I'm all these things at once</i>

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:50.950
<i>Then I only blossomed in dreams</i>

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:56.500
<i>I hid in the moon's shadow,</i> <i>but the truth is, I was crying</i>

00:22:56.710 --> 00:23:02.210
<i>The tears won't flow anymore--</i> <i>did they all dry up?</i>

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:08.760
<i>If I could forgive everything,</i> <i>maybe they'd flow again</i>

00:23:08.970 --> 00:23:16.310
<i>But these are all things I want to protect</i>

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:40.920
"The Devil and the Hero Save Sasazuka"
